Z||000000||Red Toyota MR2||01-08-2001||10:59 PM||||Hello all:<P>I own an MR2, an 86 infact.  I am looking at an 88 GT w/ a blown 2.8.  I know this motor very well, as I had one in my 86 S-10 and I know its not a very good motor.  <P>The reason I am looking at her:<P>Near perfect ext, all lights work and such<BR>OK int.<BR>Price: 150 bucks.<P>Should I pick this car up?  Is it worth it?  How much does a v-8 conversion cost?  bigger v-6?  What would you guys recomend.<P>Rick<BR>1986 Red Toyota MR2<BR>HKS exaust, header.  Ebach springs, tokico struts, R.S. Akimoto intake.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rodmcneill||01-08-2001||11:05 PM||||Let's see... a 88gt blown motor, good body,$150.00 If you don't want it let me know where it is.||||reg||14
Z||000002||RaeQwan||01-08-2001||11:07 PM||||Not that I promote violence..but grab a bat and beat the crap out of anyone else who tries to stop you from buying it.. Go Go Go <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwansig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||01-08-2001||11:53 PM||||Because of suspension improvements, the 88 is probably the best handling stock Fiero. If you get this car, you will have no trouble getting your money back out of it if you decide that you don't want it. It is easily worth $2000 in running condition, maybe more  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||2M4 Dale||01-09-2001||12:18 AM||||I disagree with you on the fact that the GM 2.8L was a bad motor.......The motor in your S10 was a bad motor. Also the Fiero engines were imroved versions (L44) high output. You can blow any motor up with enough abuse.<P>But the deal you have found on that Fiero for $150 sounds great !!!! Sell your MR2 and fix the Fiero.....all in good fun I hope you know...lol||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-09-2001||12:33 AM||||Save the $150, as you'll need it for repair's for the mr2. You may need the money sooner then you think...   lol<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000006||frontal lobe||01-09-2001||01:34 AM||||I disagree that the 2.8 is a bad engine.  It is very torquey, and I think you would find it a lot of fun and quite different than the mr2.<P>However, you could go with certain 3.1 gm engines with apparently not too much trouble with the conversion.<P>The 3.8 is a great engine for a conversion, but then you are getting into a lot more money.  Same with a v8 conversion.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||01-09-2001||02:16 AM||||Conversions options are plenty. The 3.1L and 3.4L are the easiest. Almost a direct swap. 3.4L with DOHC's is good too! A little more work but lots of power. The 3800 is good, the 3800SC (supercharged) is fantastic. As for V-8's there is the Northstar and Small Block Chevy 350's.<BR>Prices are dependant on how much work you want to do yourself. As for taking it somewhere, The average price for a 3.1/3.4L is roughly $3000. For a 3800, possibly $5000 to $8000. For V-8's your looking at $5000 to $10,000. The engine you get determines price. (the above are with low milage used engines) A "crate" engine is more expensive than a low mileage one. If you can get a donor car, that would give you a lot of the parts you need. (engine, Harness, computer,etc)  As for kit costs themselves, 3800's I've seen for about $2000 and SBC V-8's max out at about $4000. (not sure if the Northstar's have a kit or their cost)<BR>Doing the work yourself can save thousands of dollars. Just pick out an engine and many folks on the forum can assist you. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroMaster88||01-09-2001||02:21 AM||||Hell yeah man, I say go for it!!  That is a VERY good price for a 88 GT in the condition u described!  Have fun with it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||14
Z||000009||Joe4x4||01-09-2001||06:09 AM||||If you do not want it let me know .<BR>I`ll buy it $150.....steal<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/vegasdieBLK.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/animated_cat.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000010||p4n1c||01-09-2001||09:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2M4 Dale:<BR><B>I disagree with you on the fact that the GM 2.8L was a bad motor.......The motor in your S10 was a bad motor. Also the Fiero engines were imroved versions (L44) high output. You can blow any motor up with enough abuse.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree, my parents 2.8 is 12 years old with 400,000km(250,000 miles), it's only now starting to show its age.<P><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-=-<BR>-=[ Come out swingin' ]=-||||reg||1
